---

## Summary

The spec builds Photo Share as an API and a web app.

## Architecture and components

Two leaves: repos/api serves /api/ and repos/web serves the app on port 3000.

## Interfaces and contracts

POST /api/albums creates an album and returns 201 with its id.

## Data model

An album has an id, a name and an owner. A photo has an id, an album id and a file key.

## Acceptance criteria per feature

Creating an album returns 201. A missing album returns 404.

## Security considerations

The server checks the owner on every write. No password is stored in clear text.

## Testing approach

Each leaf has unit tests. The acceptance run opens repos/web.

## Decisions

- **Decided 2026-10-24:** Albums use random ids.
  Links must not be guessable.

## Deviations from the design doc

- The design asks for a reset link by SMS.
  - Where: Design, Decisions
  - Why: The leaves have no SMS service, so the reset link goes by email.
  - Owner decisions: password-reset

## Leaves

The repositories the product is built in, which Odin writes to the project's leaves.yaml:

- The runtime: niflheim-local 0.1.0
- repos/api, from helheim-go 0.1.0: The product's API.
- repos/web, from midgard-react 0.1.0: The product's web app. It consumes repos/api.
